Fixed 2026-11-20, before any result of this definition was read (owner: "file the experiments"). A screen:
each switch alone against ctl, to decide which to ship, which to tune and which to drop. classes-18 is the
gate (RULES 16); small and medium (starts 1-360) follow right after it.
Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's values in borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified and key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced;
- in ctl, no "# Phase rule: the fight:" note (lost_test 0 notes nothing of the fight).
Report per arm and per class:
- deaths and causes, final and maximum level, deepest level;
- paired rescued and newly killed against ctl (exact McNemar), and games identical to ctl (how often the
  switch acts at all);
- mean max CL and DL against ctl, with non-inferiority at the margins of borg-zoo#347 (CL -0.25, DL -0.25);
- per arm, its own notes per game ("# Phase rule: the fight:" for phase-*, the flee and stair notes for the others),
  and deaths within 500 game turns of one;
- for phase-*: Phase Doors read and "lost" against "not lost" verdicts per game.
Bin each arm (RULES 18): ship, neutral, harmful, or too rare to tell.
